%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: eclectic-types of guidance
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach in guidance is best defined as:'
    Options:
    - Strict adherence to a single theoretical orientation
    - Selective integration of techniques from various theoretical systems
    - Exclusive use of psychoanalytic methods
    - Complete rejection of all established counseling theories
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A counselor using an eclectic approach would most likely:'
    Options:
    - Apply the same techniques to all clients regardless of their problems
    - Select methods based on the client's specific needs and situation
    - Use only techniques developed within the last five years
    - Avoid using any standardized assessment tools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The primary advantage of the eclectic approach is its:'
    Options:
    - Rigid consistency in application
    - Strong theoretical purity
    - Simplicity and ease of mastery
    - Flexibility and adaptability to diverse client needs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: Which term best describes the eclectic counselor's attitude toward
      different counseling theories?
    Options:
    - Dogmatic
    - Pragmatic
    - Skeptical
    - Indifferent
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In eclectic guidance, the selection of techniques is primarily
      based on:'
    Options:
    - The counselor's personal preferences
    - What is currently most popular in the field
    - Empirical evidence and client characteristics
    - The theoretical school the counselor studied first
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach requires counselors to have:'
    Options:
    - Superficial knowledge of many theories
    - Deep understanding of multiple theoretical systems
    - Expertise in only one theoretical orientation
    - No theoretical background
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'Technical eclecticism differs from theoretical integration in
      that it:'
    Options:
    - Combines theoretical frameworks
    - Uses techniques without accepting their theoretical origins
    - Rejects all techniques from other approaches
    - Creates entirely new theories
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A key challenge of the eclectic approach is:'
    Options:
    - Lack of flexibility
    - Inability to address diverse client needs
    - Over-reliance on a single theory
    - Potential for inconsistent or haphazard application
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach is particularly valuable in today''s counseling
      practice because:'
    Options:
    - Clients' problems are becoming more homogeneous
    - It addresses the complexity and diversity of client issues
    - It simplifies counselor training requirements
    - It requires less ongoing professional development
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: Which of the following best describes a systematic eclectic approach?
    Options:
    - Random selection of techniques
    - Planned integration based on assessment and theoretical understanding
    - Using only techniques from humanistic approaches
    - Avoiding any technical integration
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A school counselor using an eclectic approach with a student having
      test anxiety might:'
    Options:
    - Use only cognitive techniques
    - Avoid using any established techniques
    - Stick exclusively to person-centered listening
    - Combine behavioral relaxation with cognitive restructuring
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach is most appropriate when:'
    Options:
    - Working with clients from similar backgrounds only
    - No single theory adequately addresses all aspects of a client's problem
    - The counselor lacks training in multiple approaches
    - The counseling agency prohibits technique integration
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: Which statement best reflects the philosophical basis of eclecticism?
    Options:
    - '"One theory fits all situations"'
    - '"Different clients and problems require different approaches"'
    - '"Techniques should never be mixed"'
    - '"Theory is more important than practical outcomes"'
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In eclectic counseling, the therapeutic relationship is typically:'
    Options:
    - Unimportant compared to technique selection
    - The only factor that matters
    - A foundation that can be enhanced by appropriate techniques
    - Avoided to maintain objectivity
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The term "integrative counseling" is often used synonymously with:'
    Options:
    - Purely behavioral counseling
    - Systematic eclectic approach
    - Single-theory adherence
    - Anti-theoretical stance
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'An eclectic counselor working with a culturally diverse client
      population would:'
    Options:
    - Apply Western techniques universally
    - Select approaches that respect and incorporate cultural factors
    - Use only techniques from the client's culture
    - Avoid considering cultural differences
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach emphasizes:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical purity above all else
    - Rejection of empirical research
    - Adherence to traditional methods
    - What works for the particular client
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A potential ethical concern in eclectic practice is:'
    Options:
    - Using only evidence-based techniques
    - Applying techniques without adequate training
    - Sticking to one theoretical orientation
    - Being too consistent with clients
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach in school settings is particularly useful
      because:'
    Options:
    - Students' problems are always simple and straightforward
    - It allows addressing academic, personal, and social issues flexibly
    - Schools typically mandate single-theory approaches
    - It requires less preparation time
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: Which factor is most important in determining technique selection
      in eclectic counseling?
    Options:
    - The counselor's comfort level
    - Colleague recommendations
    - What was most recently learned
    - Client needs and characteristics
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A student presents with both career indecision and social anxiety.
      An eclectic counselor would most likely:'
    Options:
    - Treat these as completely separate issues
    - Use trait-factor approach for career and cognitive-behavioral techniques for
      anxiety
    - Apply only psychoanalytic techniques to both issues
    - Refer the student to multiple specialists
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'When evaluating the effectiveness of eclectic practice, the most
      important criterion is:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical consistency
    - Client progress and outcomes
    - Adherence to traditional methods
    - Counselor satisfaction
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The main difference between technical eclecticism and syncretism
      is that:'
    Options:
    - Technical eclecticism is systematic while syncretism is haphazard
    - Syncretism requires more training
    - Technical eclecticism uses only behavioral techniques
    - Syncretism is more theoretically grounded
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In developing an eclectic approach, counselors should base their
      practice on:'
    Options:
    - Personal intuition alone
    - Research evidence and clinical experience
    - Popular trends in counseling
    - Client preferences exclusively
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'An eclectic counselor might combine person-centered listening
      with behavioral techniques to:'
    Options:
    - Create theoretical confusion
    - Build rapport while promoting specific behavior changes
    - Simplify the counseling process
    - Avoid dealing with emotions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The trend toward eclecticism in modern counseling practice reflects:'
    Options:
    - Growing recognition of the complexity of human problems
    - Decreasing quality of counselor training
    - Simplification of counseling techniques
    - Movement away from evidence-based practice
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A systematic eclectic counselor would typically:'
    Options:
    - Use random techniques without rationale
    - Follow a clear conceptual framework for technique selection
    - Apply the same sequence of techniques to all clients
    - Avoid assessing client characteristics
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach is particularly valuable when working with:'
    Options:
    - Clients who have single, straightforward problems
    - Complex cases involving multiple issues
    - Clients from only one cultural background
    - Problems that fit neatly into one theoretical category
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In school guidance, an eclectic approach allows counselors to:'
    Options:
    - Use the same methods for all students regardless of needs
    - Focus exclusively on academic issues
    - Avoid learning new techniques
    - Tailor their approach to individual student characteristics
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The most successful eclectic counselors are typically those who:'
    Options:
    - Have superficial knowledge of many approaches
    - Maintain strong theoretical foundations in multiple systems
    - Avoid ongoing professional development
    - Stick to techniques they learned during initial training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: A counselor using Lazarus's Multimodal Therapy (a form of technical
      eclecticism) would assess clients across how many modalities?
    Options:
    - 3
    - 5
    - 7
    - 10
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'When integrating techniques from different theories, eclectic
      counselors must be particularly mindful of:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical contradictions and client confusion
    - Using only the most complex techniques
    - Avoiding all behavioral methods
    - Sticking to one cultural perspective
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach in career counseling might involve:'
    Options:
    - Using only standardized tests
    - Combining assessment, values clarification, and decision-making strategies
    - Focusing exclusively on labor market information
    - Avoiding any personality assessment
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A key difference between eclectic and pluralistic approaches is
      that pluralism:'
    Options:
    - Emphasizes theoretical integration more strongly
    - Focuses on using only behavioral techniques
    - Rejects the idea of multiple approaches
    - Is identical to single-theory practice
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In multicultural counseling, the eclectic approach allows counselors
      to:'
    Options:
    - Impose Western techniques universally
    - Select culturally appropriate interventions
    - Avoid learning about cultural differences
    - Use only traditional healing methods
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The most significant challenge in training eclectic counselors
      is:'
    Options:
    - The extensive knowledge base required
    - The simplicity of the approach
    - Lack of available training materials
    - Resistance from clients
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'An eclectic counselor might use psychodynamic concepts to understand
      childhood influences while using cognitive-behavioral techniques to address
      current problems. This demonstrates:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical confusion
    - Systematic integration based on client needs
    - Lack of theoretical understanding
    - Inconsistent practice
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'Research on eclecticism in counseling suggests that:'
    Options:
    - Single-theory approaches are consistently superior
    - Many effective counselors describe themselves as eclectic
    - Eclecticism is declining in popularity
    - Eclectic counselors have poorer outcomes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In brief counseling situations, eclectic counselors might:'
    Options:
    - Use only long-term approaches
    - Apply the same methods as in long-term counseling
    - Avoid any technical integration
    - Select focused, time-efficient techniques
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The future of eclecticism in counseling will likely involve:'
    Options:
    - Movement toward greater theoretical purity
    - Increased emphasis on evidence-based integration
    - Abandonment of technical diversity
    - Focus on only humanistic approaches
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'A school counselor using eclectic approach with a bullied student
      might combine:'
    Options:
    - Only psychoanalytic interpretation
    - Person-centered support, social skills training, and system-level intervention
    - Exclusive focus on the victim's behavior
    - Avoidance of any emotional support
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The main criticism of unsystematic eclecticism is that it can
      become:'
    Options:
    - Too rigid and inflexible
    - Too focused on client needs
    - Overly theoretical
    - A haphazard collection of techniques
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In developing a personal eclectic approach, counselors should
      engage in:'
    Options:
    - Ongoing self-reflection and professional development
    - Strict adherence to their initial training
    - Avoidance of new techniques
    - Exclusive use of traditional methods
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The eclectic approach is particularly suitable for addressing:'
    Options:
    - Single, isolated symptoms
    - Complex, multifaceted problems
    - Only mild adjustment issues
    - Problems that fit one theoretical model
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'When using eclectic methods, counselors must ensure:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical purity above all else
    - Coherence and rationale for technique selection
    - Using only recently developed techniques
    - Avoiding any assessment of outcomes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In group counseling, an eclectic approach might involve:'
    Options:
    - Using only psychodynamic techniques
    - Applying the same methods to all groups
    - Avoiding any theoretical framework
    - Combining process-oriented and structured exercises
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'The most important factor in successful eclectic practice is:'
    Options:
    - The counselor's theoretical preferences
    - Client characteristics and needs
    - Agency policies
    - Current professional trends
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'Eclectic counselors typically view different counseling theories
      as:'
    Options:
    - Competing truths
    - Complementary tools
    - Completely irrelevant
    - Identical in application
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
  - QuestionText: 'In crisis intervention, eclectic counselors might:'
    Options:
    - Use only long-term approaches
    - Apply the same methods as in non-crisis situations
    - Avoid any technical integration
    - Combine immediate support with practical problem-solving
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: eclectic-types of guidance
